              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dēnegō, dēnegāre — \"to deny flatly; to refuse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pater mihi pecūniam dēnegāvit. Father refused me the money."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dēnegō, dēnegāre, dēnegāvī, dēnegātum. Stronger than negō: a firm no. English deny comes through French from dēnegāre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dēnegō is built from dē- and negō \"to say no\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English deny comes from it through Old French."
